Require confirmation before `gh repo delete` deletes private forks
BagToad Merged
Approved

Description

Deleting a private repository also deletes all of its forks (docs
(https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/creating-and-managing-repositories/de...)). The web UI warns about this before
you confirm: "This will also delete all 3 forks since this is a private repository." Our repo delete command
(https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/f7a06a18a91eef5c0b218b549dab64b86f36f8b9/pkg/...) doesn't. It only asks you to type the
repo name, and --yes skips even that.

The person deleting often can't see those forks. Private forks only inherit team access from their upstream, not
individual access (docs (https://docs.github.com/en/pull-requests/reference/forks#permissions-of-forks)).

gh repo delete now looks up the repo (https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/4948470b5a97a7fd839df5389527f575070ab2f8/pkg/...)
before deleting it. The new check (https://github.com/cli/cli/blob/4948470b5a97a7fd839df5389527f575070ab2f8/pkg/...)
only steps in when the repo takes its forks with it:

    // A public repo keeps its forks, and deleting a fork leaves that fork's own forks alone
    if !info.Private || info.Fork || info.ForksCount == 0 {
    return nil
    }

When it does step in:

- In a terminal, gh shows the same warning as the web UI, then asks Delete OWNER/REPO and its forks?, defaulting to No.
  It asks even with --yes.
- Without a terminal, gh exits 1 unless you also pass the new --accept-cascading-deletion-of-private-forks flag.

How did you test this change?

I built gh from trunk at f7a06a1 and from this branch at 4948470. I pointed both at a small local stand-in for the REST
API through an HTTP proxy, so no real repositories were touched. Every run used an empty config directory and a
placeholder token.

I recorded four terminal runs of this branch's build. Each one ends by printing the requests the stand-in API received.

https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a2871b54-a0a5-4851-8889-fbb3e25f1eda

Open chapters and agent notes (https://bagtoad.github.io/github-video-navigator/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.co...)

- With 3 forks, I saw the warning, answered y, and typed the repo name. The API saw the GET, then the DELETE.
- Pressing Enter at the fork prompt took the default No. gh exited with status 2 and sent no DELETE.
- With --yes, the fork prompt still appeared, but the name prompt didn't.
- With the new flag, only the name prompt appeared, and the API saw only the DELETE.

Without a terminal, trunk deleted a private repo with 3 forks and printed nothing. This branch exited with status 1
after only the GET:

    --accept-cascading-deletion-of-private-forks required when not running interactively: deleting
octo-org/secrets-vault will also delete all 3 forks since this is a private repository

I also ran these without a terminal:

- Adding the new flag skipped the lookup and sent only the DELETE.
- An internal repo with forks got the same error as a private one.
- A public repo with forks, a private fork with forks, and a private repo with no forks were still deleted.
- A missing repo and a renamed repo printed byte-identical output on both builds, with the same exit code. That includes
  the delete_repo scope hint for the missing repo. The branch now stops at the GET, so no DELETE is sent.
